 24:8 ; impersonal לְשָׂרָה לִהְיוֺת חָדַל Gen 18:11 (J); cease to be Deut 15:11 (followed by מִן ), and in poetry Judg 5:6-7 , (twice in verse); 1Sam 2:5 ; Job 14:7 ; = be lacking, fail 19:14 ; Prov 10:19 . 2 cease, leave off , followed by infinitive with לְ Gen 11:8 (J), 41:49 (E), Num 9:13 (P), 1Sam 12:23 ; 23:13 ; Jer 44:18 ; 51:30 ; Deut 23:23 ; Psa 36:4 ; Prov 19:27 ; Ruth 1:18 ; infinitive alone Isa 1:16 ; so also Hosea 8:10 , where read וְחָֽדְלוּ for ᵐ5 וַיָּחֵלּוּ Che We; followed by infinitive with מִן Exod 23:5 (JE), 1Kin 15:21 2Chr 16:5 ; followed by substantive with מִן ( cease regarding ) Isa 2:22 (but Che Du and others treat see as interpolation; omitted by ᵐ5 ), 1Sam 9:5 ; Prov 23:4 ; followed by מֵאלהים 2Chr 35:21 , i.e. leave off provoking God; Exod 14:12 (J), followed by מִמֶּנּו desist from us , let us alone; Job 7:16 ; followed by accusative 3:17 ׳ח רֹגֶז ; 14:6 have rest (i.e. cease from being troubled, see Di; compare 14:1 ); no complem. expressed, cease, forbear Judg 15:7 ; 20:28 ; Amos 7:5 ; 1Kin 22:6 , 15 2Chr 18:5 , 14 ; Jer 40:4 ; 41:8 ; Zech 11:12 ; Psa 49:9 ; Job 16:6 ; 2Chr 25:16 ; specifically of refusal to hear Ezek 2:5 , 7 ; 3:11 , 27 (all opposed to שָׁמַע ). Hoph`al Perfect (contracted) with interrogative particle הֶחֳדַלְתִּי Judg 9:9 , 11 , 13 should I be made to leave , followed by accusative (compare Kö i, 240 ff. ); ** Job 10:20 (but read here probably ᵑ6 ᵐ5 חֶלְדִּי יְמֵי Bi Bu Du); but perhaps read הֶחָדַלְתִּי , Qal Perfect Stu Be, compare, for accusative followed by, Job 3:17 .","rootNote":"a primitive root;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Kgs 15 21","keyReferences":["1Kgs 15 21","1Kgs 22 6","1Kgs 22 15","1Sam 2 5","1Sam 9 5","1Sam 12 23","1Sam 23 13","2Chr 16 5"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":59,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Kgs 15 21","book":"1Kgs","chapter":15,"verse":21,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"